{
  "_about": [
    "The scene registry: one entry per scene type, read by the bundle (the camera's class and kicks, Promo's SELF_STARTING) and by the Node tools (visual.mjs STAGINGS, tools/ci/screentext.mjs, the fx planner). Add an entry with every new scene file.",
    "cls: picture | data | text | end (the text rules' classes; end = EndCard, outside every share). clsIf: [{when, cls}] changes it by the spec's props: when {prop: value} matches a prop's value, {prop: '*'} any set value; maxWords: the scene's words must be at most that too.",
    "cam: band | free | self (src/lib/camera.tsx sceneClass: band moves inside the picture's clip, free moves the whole scene at most 1.2 %, self keeps the old 1 % drift).",
    "selfStart: the scene starts its own run after the cut when the spec gives no `at` (Promo's subtitle haptic leaves it alone).",
    "stagings: the first is the default. text: the props that draw words: path is dotted, [] maps over an array, a string element or an object's `text` is the text, * is any string prop not in `except`; max = words per item; dup false = an identity label (a caller's name, a chat contact, a notification title) that may repeat the subtitle. words: the most words the whole scene may draw (null: its own rule).",
    "dur: [min, ideal, max] seconds. moves: the camera moves the planner may pick (none: the legacy drift). kicks: dotted paths of `at` values that fire a camera kick.",
    "lookPath (Film): the prop that sets its class: look 'diagram' is data, 'illustrated' is picture.",
    "BigNumber, Callback, KineticHeadline, PhotoStory, Split, Timeline and Twist are the first batch's scenes (2026-10-06).",
    "Phase 2 (src/lib/p2.mjs, 2026-10-26): the purpose-built kit (KeywordLift, Receipt, UnitGrid, ScaleReveal, RankShift, FilmTitleCard, RouteTrace, WipeCompare, ScreenFocus, TapTrail, ScreenDeck, FreezeTag, IrisDetail, ShapeMatch) is \"picture\": a graphic made for the film's idea is a picture that explains, not a text card (KeywordLift draws the spoken line itself with \"subs\": \"inPicture\" and may open a film as its hook). TypeDive is a text transition.",
    "bleed (2026-10-06, the owner: no crop band at the top and bottom of a picture): the scene fills the whole 9:16 frame edge to edge and Promo hides the meta bar while it is on screen (src/lib/bleed.ts). true = always; a list = when one of its conditions holds ({prop or dotted.path: value, [values] (null = unset) or '*' (set)}); \"hook\" = as the film's first shot (Callback). Absent: the clean field, cut on L.graphicsTop / L.graphicsBottom (the data scenes, Phone and the other app pictures).",
    "fit (2026-10-07, the owner on v79: \"the photos are spread full screen but you cannot make them out; when nothing shows, make them smaller again\"): a photo scene bleeds only when its photos FIT the boxes its full-bleed staging fills: a list of {photo path: box name} (plus `when`, the bleed rule's conditions, for a staging's own boxes). A photo fits a box when covering it keeps at least _fit.min of the photo's width (or height) and it is not small (_fit.small, stories.mjs tooSmall); a photo that does not fit is shown whole on the clean field instead (src/lib/bleed.ts photosFit; tools/ci/stories.mjs reads the same numbers)."
  ],
  "_fit": {
    "about": "min: the least share of a photo's width (a tall box) or height (a wide box) a full-bleed crop may keep: 0.6, so a portrait or a slightly tall photo (up to 15:16) fills the 9:16 frame and a square, 4:3 or 3:2 one does not (a 4:3 keeps 42 %, a 3:2 37 %: a car becomes a bonnet). small / band: a photo that covers the old picture band (frame px) only when blown up more than 1.5 times. boxes: the aspect (w/h) of what each staging really shows: frame = the 9:16 frame (Photo bleed and cover, PhotoStory bleed and depth, Twist, a bg, Split slide); half = one half of it (Split wipe); top / foot = Split stack's two panels in the frame; window = PhotoStory's 4:5 window.",
    "min": 0.6,
    "small": 1.5,
    "band": [1080, 1110],
    "boxes": {"frame": 0.5625, "half": 0.28125, "top": 1.27, "foot": 1.02, "window": 0.8}
  },
